{"text":"Whole-outcome correction replacing unclaimed 249d113d for audit55563589/reviewf24d2b56. Builder: structural refactors of the largest modules, subject to acts-first scheduling (simplification review 55563589, findings ARCH-03, ARCH-04, ARCH-07, ARCH-09, ARCH-11, ARCH-12, LAYER-06, LAYER-08, LAYER-12). Hugh's D6 allows work any time; start when builder capacity permits or a concrete jam task needs it, preserving admission priority. (1) admission.ts: one laneTarget helper for the act prologue (nope lane-unknown is built by hand 13 times; recoveryLaneCheck, policyRefuse and holderCheck each followed by the same refused line 6 to 10 times), shared evidence helpers for review and check (:970-1011 and :1063-1151), one reviewCarryInput for propose (:748-790) and core.ts recomputeOne (:666-688), landAuthority merged with initiatorOf. (2) A lanes.ts state module replacing seven raw lane writes (admission.ts:539, 594, 659, 819, 1253; core.ts:1266, 1327) with named transitions and shared side effects. (3) Split core.ts (1,722 lines) along its section comments into landing-host, publication, notify and founding modules, as jobs.ts already does, after the alarm-steps table lands. (4) Split verify.ts verifyLog (509 lines) into readChain, retainedIndex, checkEntries and checkNeeds with a table of system-event handlers. (5) One BODY_FIELDS table per act kind in contract driving room/src/schema.ts:221-307 and client/src/room.ts:250-298 and bearer.ts:111-140. (6) A single buildEngines factory used by RoomCore and both harnesses, with test hooks in a TestServices type production configuration cannot set (room/src/ports.ts:231-263; config.ts:53-92). (7) One shared runtime-neutral tsconfig and web.d.ts so the Room stops typechecking against generated declaration files through path remaps (room/tsconfig.json paths; room typecheck script), and worker-runtime.d.ts generated once at the root. (8) Type the Publisher and checker seams: Publisher implements PublisherStub, LogRemoteStub